From b71bd1114c44492e349903984e41621c3aac424d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:24:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 61/94] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: native DSD on
 qcom,s32-as-s16-pairs DAIs

The HiBy RS6 DAC takes native DSD the way its stock HAL feeds it
(output_proxy_callback, DSD branch): both 1-bit channels bit-interleaved
in 16-bit I2S words, one byte of each channel per word, left on the
even bits, right on the odd ones, oldest bytes first. One DSD_U32
stereo frame is four such words in the same 8 bytes, so the stream to
the DSP stays S16 stereo.

Offer DSD_U32_LE and DSD_U32_BE on the qcom,s32-as-s16-pairs DAIs and
interleave each period in place in ack, as S32 is split there. Stereo
only, and only with qcom,fixed-rate: the stream must be declared at
the fixed port rate, or the DSP would resample the words like PCM.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
